{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794081711,"nonce":"niPjpYWuXw1nxAe0KNSoSiyPO28=","message":"Moved here from doc/design (story a4f7415: design documents are by aspect and describe only what is built; an unbuilt design lives on its issue).\n\n# Unbuilt: tui.md\n\nNone of these has an issue of its own; the tracker search for each found nothing.\nThe renderer's own story is the terminal-renderer one the old document named\n(`84dfbde`, whose parent is `2298f37`); the app's is `087decb` (backlog).\n\n## Actions injected into views (terminal-renderer.md, Deferred; app.md, Out of scope) — stories `84dfbde` (parent `2298f37`) and `087decb`\n\n`actions={\"Start\": start_fn}` becoming buttons on rows, cards and the show pane,\nplus a global bar for text, inputs and flow-wide actions.\nThis subsumes the `on_change` / `on_select` callback sketch:\na callback is an action the view invents a name for,\nand an action is the same thing the flow names.\nIt is the first client of the worker goroutine (now built, `tui/home.go`, where a flow run from a page runs).\nOn `show` they were to join a button row under the comment box; that button went,\nand where they land there is open again.\napp.md: the palette is where they would appear.\n\n## `work.view.split` (terminal-renderer.md, Deferred)\n\nTwo panes as one composite view.\n\n## Questions to the user (terminal-renderer.md, Deferred; comment-delete.md CD9/CD10)\n\nChoose, confirm, ask, form: how a flow asks something without a view.\n`Render` already returns a `json.RawMessage` so these can answer (`tui/tui.go`).\nA confirmation in the renderer is the one comment delete would use (CD10 lists it out of scope).\nA list that returns the human's choice (the removed `pick=True`) would come back as one of these.\n\n## Reparenting by grab (terminal-renderer.md, Navigation and editing)\n\nMoving a grabbed list item under another, writing the `expand` relation by moving it.\nLeft out of the first cut.\n\n## The mouse (terminal-renderer.md, Deferred; app.md, Out of scope)\n\nA click on a cell edits it, on a link follows it, on a tab switches to it,\nand the wheel scrolls: Bubble Tea reports clicks, and the page knows which line each thing is on.\nWhat it costs is the terminal's own drag-select, which every terminal keeps behind `Shift`\nonce a program asks for the mouse; worth writing down before it is turned on.\n\n## A recent-issues list in the finder (app.md, Out of scope) — story `087decb`\n\nWanted once the finder is used enough to show what it misses.\n\n## A multi-relation picker (terminal-renderer.md, Navigation and editing, 2026-09-29)\n\nA list of checkboxes would commit the difference as adds and removes;\nit waits on one host call that commits both as one commit.\nToday `space` on a `multi-relation` cell rings, naming `git work issue add/remove`.\n\n## No issue — `empty-groups.md`\n\n- `empty_groups` on the list, the gantt and the matrix; an explicit `group_values`;\n  a `group_query` to narrow the top-level relation case (Q1).\n  Kept in views.md's \"Not done\" as one line.","files":null}]}